93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T20:09:48-08:00","id":1500420,"title":"","content":"I imagine he would then retire to a little hut on a beach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-22T22:40:07-08:00","id":1500429,"title":"","content":"Well, a world of Eternity. A world that does not get worse but doesn't get better either.<br /> <br /> No death but no births, no damnation but no redemption, no Descension but no Ascension either.<br /> <br /> Nephandi despair, their Dark goals and Dark Gods will never happen. One of whom is The Wyrm, who is entirely purposeless if he even exists anymore and now stuck forever, The Weaver is probably happier but still not satisfied because the world still has Spirituality but can't do much about it. The Wyld definitely doesn't exists as we know it.<br /> <br /> The Void is now unable to destroy the Creation and the Light, Oblivion at the center of the Underworld stops to a halt, Wraiths aren't able to achieve Transcendece anymore but none fall to the Oblivion. No more Wraiths and locations are created since nothing is destroyed or killed anymore.<br /> <br /> That's all I can say on top of my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T01:57:16-08:00","id":1500437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Technoma</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500400-what-if-voormas-succeed?p=1500429#post1500429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, a world of Eternity. A world that does not get worse but doesn't get better either.<br /> <br /> No death but no births, no damnation but no redemption, no Descension but no Ascension either.<br /> <br /> Nephandi despair, their Dark goals and Dark Gods will never happen. One of whom is The Wyrm, who is entirely purposeless if he even exists anymore and now stuck forever, The Weaver is probably happier but still not satisfied because the world still has Spirituality but can't do much about it. The Wyld definitely doesn't exists as we know it.<br /> <br /> The Void is now unable to destroy the Creation and the Light, Oblivion at the center of the Underworld stops to a halt, Wraiths aren't able to achieve Transcendece anymore but none fall to the Oblivion. No more Wraiths and locations are created since nothing is destroyed or killed anymore.<br /> <br /> That's all I can say on top of my head.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That has always been my impression regarding his goal, he wanted an absolute stasis or as you ave put it, &quot;a world of eternity&quot;, basically because he was afraid of dying. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine he would then retire to a little hut on a beach. </div> </div> </div>Hahaha this<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-23T11:08:39-08:00","id":1500462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500400-what-if-voormas-succeed?p=1500437#post1500437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That has always been my impression regarding his goal, he wanted an absolute stasis or as you ave put it, &quot;a world of eternity&quot;, basically because he was afraid of dying.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, let me get the quote for it in fact.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ToJ 56</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Voormas fears death, an ironic thing indeed for a<br /> mage in the throes of Jhor. He wants more than just<br /> long life. What terrifies the archmage is the end of the<br /> Cycle itself, when he will answer for centuries\u2019 worth<br /> of dark karma.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ToJ 84</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Helekar\u2019s master thwarts Ascension out of compassion<br /> \u2014 and fear. By unhinging the Wheel of Creation,<br /> he hopes to re-create the world in his own image: a<br /> Destroyer that never kills; a Black Mother who never<br /> gives birth. This would be the supreme act of necrosynthesis:<br /> unity between the life and death principle.<br /> Voormas\u2019 Tapestry would be world without growth,<br /> but without loss. The dead and the living would be<br /> a part of one indestructible whole. Awakening would<br /> be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}